<section id="last-moat" class="moat section">
  <div class="container moat__inner">
    <p class="eyebrow">The last moat</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">AI can take the corner office. It can't mount the TV.</h2>

    <div class="moat__copy">
      <p>Walk through any downtown tower right now and you're looking at the work AI is learning fastest. Reports. Scheduling. Bookkeeping. Research. The towers are handing that work to agents like MoneyPenny. I put mine to work for my trade business. She's my right hand. She runs the office while I run the jobs.</p>
      <p>Now ask her to mount a TV over a stone fireplace.</p>
      <p>She can't. AI can't plumb a house, run a circuit, build a deck, or get a roof on before the rain. That work still takes someone who knows the craft and shows up to do it. The need for it isn't shrinking, and the number of people who do it well is.</p>
      <p>For years the trades got sold as the backup plan. Now they're the part of the economy software can't reach. The people who do that work should be the ones who get paid for it. This is the moment to claim that.</p>
      <p>I stepped in front of that wave early. I built The Mounting Man in the Twin Cities by getting very good at the part most tradesmen skip: advertising, and pricing the expertise instead of the hours. At some point I did the math against a well-known Twin Cities professional, the kind of career people point to when they tell you to make something of yourself. I realized I was probably out-earning him. Not because mounting TVs matters more than what he does. Because I learned to market my work and price it like it mattered.</p>
      <p class="moat__proof">My best day was $6,458.10. My best month was $59,798.23. My best year was $512,022.13.</p>
      <p>Skill alone isn't the moat. Plenty of great installers are broke. The moat is the skill plus the business behind it: ads that bring in the right customers, SEO that keeps them coming, and AI that handles the office so you stay on the job. The operators who put those together will own the next decade in their market.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

